abstract: >-
  A cross-jurisdictional causal evaluation of carrot-policy mechanisms for
  low-carbon hydrogen project survival. Using project-level survival analysis
  of 1,354 Blue and Green hydrogen projects (S&P Global, 2010-2024), this
  research identifies the differential effects of four major policy types
  (US Section 45Q, EU Innovation Fund, UK Track-1, China 14th Five-Year Plan)
  and introduces offtake commitment as an under-appreciated mechanism through
  which subsidies operate. Findings are grounded in a Dixit-Pindyck (1994)
  real-options framework distinguishing V/I-boost vs sigma-attack channels.
